## Use cases

- Browser or Electron log viewers with host-owned pause/history controls.
- Interactive Electron PTYs whose trusted host owns command execution and lifecycle.
- ANSI/Unicode output previews that do not need any process privileges.

## Accessibility

- Supply a localized `labels.ariaLabel`; it labels both the terminal region and the input textarea.
- xterm screen-reader support is enabled. Read-only output still allows text selection and copying.
- Keep `autoFocus` off unless opening an explicit interactive terminal is the user's action. Log updates must not move focus.
